  "details": "There have been many times when I've ended up in a group-only instance without realizing my friends couldn’t join me, or I’ve been in a friends+ instance thinking it was private, only to be surprised by someone’s sudden visit.\n\nI know there’s a notification when you join a world that says something like \"You joined a friends+ instance,\" but 95% of the time I don’t even notice it. The issue with this notification is that it appears right when you're going from the sensory-deprived void to a new environment filled with loading people, their voices, banners with rules, etc. - so this notification has to compete for your attention with all these other stimuli happening at once.\n\nOn the other hand, while you're in the loading void, there's nothing else demanding your attention, making it the perfect time to review your access and social settings without distraction. It could also help in those moments when you forget to change your status.",
